So far Northgard is the best RTS I've played in a long, long time, there are several pros that make this game very enjoyable, tho there are cons aswell, which I believe might be redone in a later development, as the game is still in EA.
Pros:
-Clear rules of the game;
-Random map generator;
-Graphics play very well with music;
-Well optimised;
Cons:
-I feel like AI is a little bit too predictible;
-Talking AI I miss some kind of diplomatic things;
-How about making the first tile we get on map as our "root tile" which would have more development options? e.g. building a wall round the tile to make it look "citisih"
-Would love to see more trading options

There's something really nostalgic about this game that I can't quite put my finger on, even though it's my first time playing it. The visuals are breathtaking and the movements are fluid. No cheap jumpscares or any such things. This also reminds me about that horror flash game called Exmortis, except that it's much better and less spookier. c;
Also, THANK GOD that you respawn right where you stopped last instead of restarting the whole puzzle (is that how you call it?). I don't deny that a lot of work went into the second chapter/level, but I still wasn't impressed. And it's where it occurred to me that the man's breathings could have been a little more realistic or spiritish. But again, these are details, details!
The screams in Hell were not bad at all, but could be improved for maximum realism. xD Otherwise, I want to congratulate the team for this piece of art. Much love and keep up the good work!

So here is my review;
I really enjoy the game. It is extremely addictive and interesting to play. It is a game that gets you thinking.
Here is my beg and plea to the game devs;
Please implement a leave-ban system like LoL or something. It really ruins the game completely when you have people get killed and instantly just leave. Especially if that player is a Jester or a Medium or anyone as a matter of fact. Please devs? This is my only gripe with the game currently.

Yoooo, zup? :D
Well, gotta say that i beat every level and got every achievement in something like 1 hour.
It's kinda weird but it's just like that. Anyways it's really fun to play, that's for sure.
You will understand it when you start playing. I found some achievements kinda funny, i mean, the way you get them.
PROS:
- Not boring at all;
- Good value;
- Nice artwork;
- Nice puzzles;
- Variety of levels;
- Way more levels than the previous Zup's;
After you play this game you'll want to buy the other Zup's as i did.
I hope they keep doing more games like this, i'm ready for Zup 6,7,8,9 and Infinite :D
MY RATING: 10/10

I really liked this game! I wasn't disappointed after waiting for nearly(or maybe a full) year for it to come out. Met my expectations and nearly exeeded them. I didn't expect it to be so creative and just.....friggin awesome. I'm kinda sad that it's over and that I beat it already. If only it were longer~..!
9/10 because it felt so short ; - ;
But yeah, it'd be great if they made a second one. I would be glad to support the creators of this game again and I'm happy I did this time instead of downloading it anywhere else for free. If you like Psychological Horror Point-and-Click games, for the love of peanuts, PLAY THIS GAME!

