Played on Win8 tablet (i5, HD4000):
No glitches or lags whatsoever, the game runs smoothly and great on 1080p (HD4000). The controls are staggering because the game reads the touchscreen as a mouse, and there's no multitouch support for the same reason, but that's not a huge problem. It's fun and plays nice on the go.
- Works with touchscreen;
- Doesn't support multitouch;
- Requires a keyboard once to enter a name;
- Runs smoothly.
